parts.text:
The codemod wrapped array expressions in `new View[] { arrayExpr }`, causing `View[]` element (nested array) which is not a View. It should have used the array directly as the children argument, not as an element.

For `children.addAll(rows.toArray(...))` only statements, our parser should have emitted `children(ARG.toArray(...))` direct, but it seems it treated `add` with arg `rows.toArray(new View[0])` (single add) and wrapped in array literal. Wait, the original code likely was:
```java
ScrollView.children(VStack.children(rows.toArray(new View[0])))
```
The previous codemod (block form) turned this into:
```java
ScrollView.children(childScope1 -> {
